  "prefLabel": "Fis 601.10 Weir",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Fis 601.10 “Weir” means a fixed position fish trap consisting of a lead of net strung from poles, usually wooden, with a pocket of net within which the fish are contained.\n\nSource. #12652, eff 10-27-18 (formerly Fis 601.04)",
